======================================================================================================================
VERDICT
======================================================================================================================
  The clock is fixable: an exponential-wall K keeps the charge cold at every epoch (c_s <= 3 km/s), the CMB and the z = 3 forest are
  Newtonian to better than 10% at every k, and the DBI pin was a DBI artefact.  The candidate is not: once the charge is cold it is
  ballistic (no quasistatic well exists, e^1000), the kernel boosts it like everything else, and the framework's own accretion lands
  27-55 M_b inside 250 kpc, excluded on the KiDS isolated rail at Delta chi2 >= +100 -- the same number that closed AeST.  Moving the
  clock dust to the unboosted metric (Newtonian accretion) is excluded by the KiDS stellar-mass bins as well.  Inside one metric the
  fix moves CCNL from dead-on-the-forest to dead-on-lensing.  The one door left is two-sector: the dark charge in a second metric that
  sources the visible potential at linear order and is screened in wells -- the Blanchet class, whose health is the open assertion.

